Title: THE LAST FRAME
Author: SceneGraph AI - Demonstration screenplay

INT. EDITING LAB - DAY

A half-finished student film flickers on a monitor. A deadline glows red.

MIRA
The footage is missing. We only have two days.

ARJUN
Then we'll find the missing card.

INT. COLLEGE CORRIDOR - DAY

Mira and Arjun search through their equipment bags.

MIRA
You had the camera yesterday.

ARJUN
I gave it to Dev after class.

EXT. CAMPUS COURTYARD - DAY

DEV
I left the camera in the equipment room.

MIRA
We'll get it after lunch.

INT. EQUIPMENT ROOM - NIGHT

The door is locked and the lights flicker.

DEV
The key should be with the supervisor.

INT. CAFETERIA - DAY

The students gather around a notebook.

TARA
We have a backup. Check the memory cards.

ARJUN
I'll run the checksum now.

INT. EDITING LAB - NIGHT

Mira reviews the corrupted footage frame by frame.

MIRA
This one frame isn't corrupted.

TARA
That's where we start rebuilding.

EXT. CAMPUS COURTYARD - DAY

A small team sets up a makeshift shooting station.

DEV
The morning light will disappear soon.

TARA
We're ready. Sound rolling.

INT. CLASSROOM - DAY

Arjun draws an alternative shot plan on a whiteboard.

ARJUN
We'll shoot the ending before the beginning.

MIRA
As long as we track continuity.

INT. EQUIPMENT ROOM - DAY

Tara returns a lens case to the shelf.

TARA
Everything is labeled this time.

DEV
Let's keep it that way.

EXT. CAMPUS COURTYARD - EVENING

The crew captures one final shot as the sun dips.

MIRA
That's the frame we needed.

ARJUN
We actually made it.

INT. EDITING LAB - DAY

The computer starts rendering.

TARA
We can export before submission.

DEV
Don't touch anything!

INT. AUDITORIUM - NIGHT

The short film plays to a quiet audience.

ARJUN
I can't believe it's on the screen.

MIRA
We didn't give up.
